WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.036
This morning, CNN has learned

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:04.604
that this woman has been detained

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:06.740
by Russian authorities in connection

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:07.874
with Sunday's deadly

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:10.043
bombing at a cafe in Saint Petersburg.

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:10.744
Here is the moment

00:00:10.744 --> 00:00:13.113
we want to show you that it injured

00:00:13.113 --> 00:00:14.514
the moment of the blast.

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:16.049
You see it right there.

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:17.517
It injured more than 30

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:18.852
people, killed a prominent

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:19.719
military blogger

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:20.520
known to be

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.322
a major supporter

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:24.324
of Russia's invasion of Ukraine.

00:00:24.324 --> 00:00:25.892
The Kremlin has said that Ukraine

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:27.994
could be behind the attack.

00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:28.528
However, no

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:29.963
evidence has been presented yet

00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:31.297
to support that claim.

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:31.865
And then there

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:34.801
is this newly released video which shows

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:36.770
the same woman now

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:37.370
under arrest

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:39.672
outside the cafe that same day

00:00:39.973 --> 00:00:40.840
carrying a box.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:42.742
And Russian media have also put out

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:44.210
photographs of that woman

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:46.479
standing near the blogger who was killed.

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:48.915
This was just inside the cafe

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:51.084
right before the explosion.

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:52.886
CNN's Fred Pleitgen is following

00:00:52.886 --> 00:00:54.054
all of this from Berlin.

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:55.055
He's joining us now.

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:55.422
Fred,

00:00:55.422 --> 00:00:56.723
what are we learning about

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:58.291
this woman who has been

00:00:58.291 --> 00:00:59.325
who has just been detained

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:03.730
Well, our name is Daria Trepova.

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:04.497
And right now,

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:06.232
this is an anti-terror investigation.

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:07.367
As far as the Russians are concerned.

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:08.101
It was quite interesting

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:10.003
because just a couple of hours ago,

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:10.437
the Russians

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:11.871
put out a video of her

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:13.940
apparently being interrogated

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:15.375
by that anti-terror committee.

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:16.109
And she was asked, look,

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:17.277
do you know why you're here?

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:18.344
And she said, yes,

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:20.346
because I gave the figurine to 

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:21.214
Vladlen Tatarsky.

00:01:21.214 --> 00:01:22.115
You, of course, is that

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:23.883
military blogger who was killed.

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:25.485
She was then asked

00:01:25.485 --> 00:01:26.152
who she got

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:27.087
that figurine from,

00:01:27.087 --> 00:01:28.521
and she said that she didn't want to say

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:30.090
at that point in time.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:30.523
So clearly,

00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:31.958
they are already confronting her

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:32.392
with that.

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:34.227
And we did see those photographs also

00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:35.328
on that video of her

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:37.330
apparently going inside that cafe

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:38.531
with that box

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:40.533
We also have an eyewitness testimony

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:41.334
of someone

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:44.237
who saw her give that to Vlad in tatters.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:44.971
I want to read you what

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:45.839
that eyewitness said.

00:01:45.839 --> 00:01:46.873
She said, quote,

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:48.675
When she gifted him the figurine

00:01:48.675 --> 00:01:49.709
she went to sit

00:01:49.709 --> 00:01:51.711
in a different place at the window,

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:53.213
so obviously away from the stage

00:01:53.213 --> 00:01:54.647
where the explosion took place.

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:55.915
The host at the stage

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:57.617
took the figurine from the box

00:01:57.617 --> 00:01:59.219
and showcased it Vlad,

00:01:59.219 --> 00:02:00.620
and held it for a bit.

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.489
They put it back and shortly

00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:04.524
after the explosion happened.

00:02:04.524 --> 00:02:05.792
That's sort of a run down.

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:07.494
What happened then?

00:02:07.494 --> 00:02:10.130
Her husband dropped off his husband.

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:11.865
He came out earlier today

00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:12.499
and he said

00:02:12.499 --> 00:02:14.434
he believes that she was framed, that

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:16.202
she didn't know what was inside

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:18.304
the figurine that she gifted to that

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:19.172
military blogger.

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:19.672
Obviously,

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:20.473
you already saying that

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:21.241
the Russians are saying

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:22.742
that the Ukrainians might be behind.

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:24.344
The Ukrainians are already denying that.

00:02:24.344 --> 00:02:25.378
They're also saying

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:26.012
that they believe

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:28.715
that she had contact with Alexei Navalny

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:31.317
Navalny's organization, of course,

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:32.819
the opposition leader.

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:34.087
That organization has also

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:35.188
denied that as well, Kate.

00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:37.023
What else are you learning

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:40.360
about the military blogger who was killed

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:43.029
So, I think I think one of the things

00:02:43.029 --> 00:02:44.063
to make clear to our viewers

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:45.832
is I think military blogger is probably

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:47.267
an understatement on the face of it.

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:48.968
That's what Vlad and to task was,

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.670
he was very prominent in that sphere.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.605
He had more than 500,000 followers

00:02:52.605 --> 00:02:53.540
on Telegram.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:54.908
But these military bloggers

00:02:54.908 --> 00:02:57.710
essentially are supporters of the war

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:58.711
in Ukraine.

00:02:58.711 --> 00:02:59.546
And one of the thing

00:02:59.546 --> 00:03:00.580
that's interesting about them

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:02.549
is that they embed quite frequently

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:03.783
with Russian forces there.

00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:05.552
It's also something that Vlad into task

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:06.519
did as well.

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:08.254
But they are also among

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:09.122
the few people

00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:09.989
who are allowed

00:03:09.989 --> 00:03:11.090
to criticize

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:13.092
the way that the war is being led.

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:14.294
It doesn't mean they're against it.

00:03:14.294 --> 00:03:15.428
In fact, they are for it.

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:16.663
But they want the Russians

00:03:16.663 --> 00:03:19.199
to be even tougher and be more brutal.

00:03:19.232 --> 00:03:20.533
That's one of the things that Vlad

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:21.167
and the task

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:22.035
he also did

00:03:22.035 --> 00:03:22.635
and one of the things

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:24.337
that he notoriously did

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:25.772
is when Russia announced

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:26.573
the annexation

00:03:26.573 --> 00:03:28.708
of four territories in Ukraine,

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:29.676
He essentially said

00:03:29.676 --> 00:03:31.511
that the Russians would kill anyone

00:03:31.511 --> 00:03:32.745
who stood in their way

00:03:32.745 --> 00:03:34.080
and would loot any one

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.348
that they wanted to as well.

00:03:35.348 --> 00:03:37.016
So certainly he was someone

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:37.817
who was hated

00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:38.985
by the Ukrainians,

00:03:38.985 --> 00:03:40.320
definitely someone

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:41.988
who was in favor of the war,

00:03:41.988 --> 00:03:44.023
but also someone who criticized the way

00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:45.959
that the Russian military is doing it

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:46.826
for the way for

00:03:46.826 --> 00:03:48.995
for allegedly not being tough enough

00:03:49.329 --> 00:03:50.263
and knowing all that.

00:03:50.263 --> 00:03:50.997
I mean, this happened

00:03:50.997 --> 00:03:52.232
in Saint Petersburg.

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:54.000
Are you hearing anything about how,

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:57.770
if and how his death is impacting

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:59.706
others like him, other supporters

00:03:59.706 --> 00:04:00.607
of Russia's

00:04:00.607 --> 00:04:02.642
military operation in the invasion

00:04:02.642 --> 00:04:04.644
from within Russia, yet

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:07.280
Yes, supporters.

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:07.780
And when

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:08.681
you mentioned supporters,

00:04:08.681 --> 00:04:10.350
I think it's important to point out

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:12.385
that it's supporters like him, bloggers,

00:04:12.385 --> 00:04:13.253
but also people who,

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:14.287
for instance,

00:04:14.287 --> 00:04:15.021
support the war

00:04:15.021 --> 00:04:16.990
in a more ideological way as well.

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:18.157
One of the things that we have to keep in

00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:20.159
mind is that this is the second time

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:22.862
that a very prominent pro-war supporter

00:04:23.029 --> 00:04:24.364
has been assassinated.

00:04:24.364 --> 00:04:25.498
In August of last year,

00:04:25.498 --> 00:04:27.667
I was in Moscow when Daria Dugin,

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:29.302
who's the daughter of Alexander

00:04:29.302 --> 00:04:31.271
Dugin, one of the main sort of ideologues

00:04:31.271 --> 00:04:32.372
who many say

00:04:32.372 --> 00:04:34.307
delivers the ideological foundation

00:04:34.307 --> 00:04:36.209
for Russia's war in Ukraine,

00:04:36.209 --> 00:04:38.311
She was assassinated on a street

00:04:38.544 --> 00:04:40.280
in Moscow and hit by a car bomb.

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:41.481
And now for the second time,

00:04:41.481 --> 00:04:42.582
certainly this is something

00:04:42.582 --> 00:04:44.350
that will send chills down

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:44.917
the spines

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:46.886
of many of the prominent people

00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:48.321
who support Vladimir Putin's war

00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:49.489
in Ukraine Kate.

00:04:49.489 --> 00:04:50.323
So interesting.

00:04:50.323 --> 00:04:52.158
Fred, thank you very much.

00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:53.393
And John, there are a lot of questions

00:04:53.393 --> 00:04:54.961
still about what's happened here,

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:55.995
but there's also a lot

00:04:55.995 --> 00:04:56.763
this isn't the only news

00:04:56.763 --> 00:04:57.597
coming out of Russia right now.

00:04:57.597 --> 00:04:58.831
No, that's exactly right, Kate,

00:04:58.831 --> 00:05:00.733
because just in Russian,

00:05:00.733 --> 00:05:02.135
state media is reporting

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:02.769
that Wall Street

00:05:02.769 --> 00:05:03.436
Journal reporter

00:05:03.436 --> 00:05:05.672
Evan Gursky has filed an appeal

00:05:05.672 --> 00:05:07.040
to his arrest, Gursky,

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:08.741
that faces up to 20 years in prison

00:05:08.741 --> 00:05:10.476
after being arrested there last week.

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:11.611
He is the first U.S.

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:12.312
journalist

00:05:12.312 --> 00:05:13.713
to be detained by Moscow

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:16.082
on espionage charges since the Cold War.

00:05:16.516 --> 00:05:17.250
Secretary of State

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:18.351
Antony Blinken spoke

00:05:18.351 --> 00:05:19.452
with the Russian Foreign Minister

00:05:19.452 --> 00:05:21.854
Sergei Lavrov, to demand his release.

00:05:22.121 --> 00:05:24.157
Lavrov blamed Washington

00:05:24.157 --> 00:05:25.224
and the Western press

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:26.793
for politicizing the arrests

00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:27.126
and said

00:05:27.126 --> 00:05:28.895
the fate of Kovic would be determined

00:05:28.895 --> 00:05:30.430
by a Russian court.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:31.030
Secretary of State

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:32.098
Blinken also called

00:05:32.098 --> 00:05:32.899
for the release of Paul

00:05:32.899 --> 00:05:34.801
Whalen, who is serving a 16 year

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:36.703
sentence for espionage, which of course

00:05:36.703 --> 00:05:38.905
Whalen and the U.S. disputes.

00:05:38.905 --> 00:05:39.872
Blinken and Lavrov

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:41.574
have only spoken three times

00:05:41.574 --> 00:05:43.142
since Russia invaded Ukraine.

00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:44.711
Each of those calls

00:05:44.711 --> 00:05:46.412
focused on trying to free

00:05:46.412 --> 00:05:47.814
detained Americans.

